{
    "background_story": "In ancient Egyptian lore, Jiraiya was a powerful and mysterious entity, said to be a mummy with extraordinary abilities. According to legend, Jiraiya was once a great pharaoh who had mastered the dark arts, allowing him to cheat death and preserve his body for eternity. Wrapped in linen bandages and adorned with golden amulets, Jiraiya roamed the desert sands, seeking justice and protecting the innocent. His powers were said to be boundless, able to control the sands, summon storms, and bend the will of others to his command. Despite his fearsome reputation, Jiraiya was a just and fair guardian, using his abilities to defend the people of Egypt from harm. His legend lived on for centuries, inspiring generations to come.",
